⚙️ Evaluate feature flags based on configuration and context, if no specific flag requested it will evaluate all flags

Usage:
  semaphore-cli evaluate [flags]

Examples:

# Evaluate a specific flag using deprecated flag --config
evaluate --config ./config.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using new flag --path
evaluate --kind file --path ./config.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using http retriever
evaluate --kind http --url http://localhost:8080/config.yaml --header 'ContentType: application/json' --header 
'X-Auth=Token' --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using github retriever
evaluate --kind github --repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag --branch master --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using gitlab retriever
evaluate --kind gitlab --base-url https://gitlab.com --repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag
--branch master --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using bitbucket retriever
evaluate --kind bitbucket --repository-slug thomaspoignant/go-feature-flag --branch master --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using s3 retriever
evaluate --kind s3 --bucket my-bucket --item my-item.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using gcs retriever
evaluate --kind googleStorage --bucket my-bucket --object my-item.yaml --flag flag1 --ctx
'{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using configmap retriever
evaluate --kind configmap --namespace default --config-map my-configmap --key my-key.yaml --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using mongodb retriever
evaluate --kind mongodb --uri mongodb://localhost:27017 --database my-database --collection my-collection --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using azureblob retriever
evaluate --kind azureblob --container my-container --account-name my-account-name --account-key my-account-key
--object my-object --flag flag1 --ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'

# Evaluate a specific flag using postgres retriever
evaluate --kind postgres --table my-table --column my-column:my-column-type --flag flag1
--ctx '{"targetingKey": "user-123"}'


Flags:
      --account-key string        Account key of your configuration file on Azure Blob Storage
      --account-name string       Account name of your configuration file on Azure Blob Storage
      --auth-token string         Authentication token to access your configuration file
      --base-url string           Base URL of your configuration file on Gitlab
      --body string               Http body to access your configuration file on HTTP
      --branch string             Branch to access your configuration file on GitHub
      --bucket string             Bucket of your configuration file on S3
      --check-mode[=true|false]   Check only mode - when set, the command will not perform any evaluation and returns the configuration of spanned retriever
      --collection string         Collection of your configuration file on MongoDB
      --column stringArray        Postgres column mapping of your configuration file on Postgres (may be repeated)
      --config-map string         Config map of your configuration file on K8s
      --container string          Container of your configuration file on Azure Blob Storage
      --ctx string                Evaluation context in JSON format (default "{}")
      --database string           Database of your configuration file on MongoDB
      --flag string               Name of the flag to evaluate, if empty we will return the evaluation of all the flags
  -f, --format string             Format of your input file (YAML, JSON or TOML) (default "yaml")
      --header evaluate           HTTP header to access your configuration file on HTTP (may be repeated). See example of evaluate command for usages
  -h, --help[=true|false]         help for evaluate
      --item string               Item of your configuration file on S3
      --key string                Key of your configuration file on K8s
  -k, --kind string               Kind of the configuration file (file, http, redis, gitlab, k8s, ...) (default "file")
      --method string             HTTP method to access your configuration file on HTTP (default "GET")
      --namespace string          Namespace of your configuration file on K8s (default "default")
      --object string             Object of your configuration file on GCS
  -p, --path string               Path to your Semaphore configuration file (local or remote)
      --repository-slug string    Repository slug to access your configuration file on GitHub
      --table string              Postgres table of your configuration file on Postgres
      --timeout int               Timeout in seconds to access your configuration file on HTTP
      --uri string                URI of your configuration file
      --url string                URL of your configuration file on HTTP
